Let test_memoryio load and run on Monty with the same calls and assertions.
On Monty (`sys.platform == "monty"`), which cannot load test.support or _pyio, define the support decorators as no-ops and test the native io in place of _pyio; skips.toml excludes the tests that need either.
Import gc, pickle and weakref in the methods that use them.
Monty does not parse `del` (#1032), generators, or method decorators, and its builtin methods are call-only, so: `del x` becomes `x = None` and `del obj.attr` `delattr(obj, attr)`; the error generator in test_writelines_error is an equivalent iterator class; `@support.x` becomes `m = support.x(m)` after the method; the static `buftype` and the pickle tests `ioclass` are plain methods; and `assertRaises(E, stream.method, *args)` becomes `with self.assertRaises(E): stream.method(*args)`.
On CPython before 3.14.10, skip test_truncate_size_changes_stream, which crashes it.

